{
    "description": [
        "Ids that Snapmaker Orca 2.4 shipped and that this tree keeps on purpose, although they do not follow",
        "the rules check enforces (setting_id = generate_preset_setting_id(vendor, type, name), no setting_id on",
        "a base, filament_id = an OF mint). The loader keys the existing presets, projects and printers on them:",
        "a filament without filament_id takes its own setting_id as filament_id (PresetBundle::commit_vendor_preset),",
        "PresetBundle::full_config writes those ids into filament_ids (G-code header and 3MF), the Snapmaker and",
        "Moonraker printer agents match trays by filament_id, and a user preset records its parent's setting_id",
        "as base_id. Changing one changes all of that for every Snapmaker Orca 2.4 user.",
        "Each entry exempts exactly one file with exactly that id; a new preset, or an entry whose id changes,",
        "is held to the rules. Entries may only be removed. Keys are paths inside the vendor folder."
    ],
